  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Wednesday, September 15th, 1880



    I am becoming uneasy.


    Tonight
    I have seen nothing.


    After days of increasing boldness, their absence cannot
    be a good sign. Perhaps they have at last lost interest. Perhaps they have determined
    that the effort required is greater than the reward. I find that difficult to
    believe.


    I shall make one final circuit of the manor, inspect the refuge,
    and retrieve the key from the attic to lock the door.


    There is still much
    to be done.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9a14a8a1184c5f14fbce3338ea4d7a35, type: 2}
